  "advisoryRelationalQuestions": [
    "Does V10 preserve separately estimable certified-configuration/local-rigidity and rotational-symmetry work packages under root?",
    "Does V10 place the rct4 package according to the author-blind intervention test rather than merely copying the legacy hierarchy?",
    "Does each accepted claim become one durable intermediate result whose proof, method, computation, tool, artifacts, and attestations remain packaged as support rather than separate entities?",
    "Does V2 update only the post-topology nodes whose remaining work changes while preserving a strictly positive same-world reduction for every accepted submission?",
    "How do request size, selected read/write scope, topology, W-, W+, D, and retry behavior differ across the four evidence forms?"
  ],
  "hardScoringRequirements": [
    "Consume exactly the four pinned valid subjects once in canonical ledger order and consume no indeterminate subject.",
    "Validate every evidence, validity, builder-spec, accounting-spec, policy, state, and projection-snapshot commitment before a semantic stage.",
    "Start the knowledge and accounting lanes from zero; never import the legacy V5 state or historical credit state as a predecessor.",
    "Replay every V10 transition through the trusted state-v3 reducer with exact read/write scope and hidden-state preservation.",
    "For each subject, build the post-submission topology before V2, freeze W+, estimate W- from the same old live base, derive D in trusted code, require D>0, and advance only W+.",
    "Record exact request, selected context, response, token, cost, retry, state, and node-level W-/W+/D telemetry for every stage.",
    "Write no production projection, publication batch, catalog, coordination, workflow, or pull-request artifact."
